(### Origins and release chronology) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Commodore International's original AmigaDOS disk filesystem shipped in 1985) Tj
T* (with AmigaOS 1.0; the designation OFS \(Old or Original File System\) was) Tj
T* (applied retrospectively. It was designed around floppy disks. FFS \(Fast File) Tj
T* (System, also called AFFS in Linux\) was introduced with AmigaOS 1.3 in 1988,) Tj
T* (handler v34. FFS removes the 24-byte per-data-block OFS header, permitting) Tj
T* (direct transfer of whole payload blocks and increasing capacity and) Tj
T* (sequential throughput on hard disks. OFS retains type, owner, sequence,) Tj
T* (length, next-block and checksum fields; FFS raw payload blocks do not. This) Tj
T* (affects salvage as well as performance.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (AmigaOS 1.0-1.2: original DOS0. AmigaOS 1.3 \(1988, v34\): DOS1 and) Tj
T* (compatibility with DOS0. AmigaOS 2.0 \(1990, v37; international profiles) Tj
T* (documented for 2.04\): DOS2/DOS3, ROM-integrated FFS. AmigaOS 3.0 \(1992,) Tj
T* (v39\): DOS4/DOS5. AmigaOS 3.1 \(1993, v40/v40.1\): last Commodore FFS) Tj
T* (generation. Later third-party v44 TD64 patches and licensed v45 NSD handler) Tj
T* (releases \(AmigaOS 3.5/3.9, Haage & Partner\) extended device addressing.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In the early 2000s, Olaf Barthel's FFS2 evolved the handler for MorphOS) Tj
T* (\(v46\) and AmigaOS 4 \(v50\), including DOS6/DOS7 long-name modes. These are) Tj
T* (OFS and FFS format variants, not a new unrelated on-disk filesystem.) Tj
T* (Hyperion's AmigaOS 3.1.4 \(September 2018\) shipped v46 with multiple) Tj
T* (large-device interfaces; 3.1.4.1 \(July 2019\) updated the disk components.) Tj
T* (AmigaOS 3.2 \(May 2021\) shipped the v47 generation with further refinements.) Tj
T* (Version numbers are handler lineage, not the fourth DOSType byte; versions) Tj
T* (from distinct branches are not a single monotonically ordered release train.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### DOSTypes and namespace compatibility) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (DOSType is the binary sequence 44 4F 53 xx, not ASCII 'DOS0'. DOS0: original) Tj
T* (OFS; DOS1: original FFS; DOS2: OFS International; DOS3: FFS International;) Tj
T* (DOS4: OFS Directory Cache; DOS5: FFS Directory Cache; DOS6: OFS Long Name) Tj
T* (File System \(LNFS\); DOS7: FFS LNFS. Even types own OFS header-bearing) Tj
T* (payload; odd types own FFS raw payload. DOS2/3 use international Latin-1) Tj
T* (case folding; DOS4/5 inherit it and add DCFS; DOS6/7 inherit international) Tj
T* (folding but do not use directory cache. Classic names are limited to 30) Tj
T* (on-disk bytes; some sources count 31 including length/terminator. LNFS has a) Tj
T* (107-character API envelope; Hyperion recommends a 106-character) Tj
T* (interoperable writer limit. Volume labels remain 30 bytes. The 112-byte NaC) Tj
T* (field stores length-prefixed name and comment; overflow comments use type-64) Tj
T* (blocks. International case folding is not Unicode folding.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (International mode changes equivalence/hashing for accented Latin-1 letters,) Tj
